<title>USA: U.S. weekend box office chart -- Aug. 15-17.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekend box office chart -- Aug. 15-17.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the final data for the top 10 movies at the Aug. 15-17 box office, according to Exhibitor Relations Co. on Monday.</p>
<p>    Film			Three-day gross    Cumulative Gross</p>
<p> 1. Cop Land		    $13,510,482	 $  ----</p>
<p> 2. Air Force One	     $12,350,122	 $130,353,620</p>
<p> 3. Conspiracy Theory	 $12,309,562	 $ 40,668,584</p>
<p> 4. Event Horizon	     $ 9,511,915	 $  ----</p>
<p> 5. Spawn			 $ 4,986,874	 $ 46,650,381</p>
<p> 6. George of the Jungle    $ 4,813,639	 $ 84,580,796</p>
<p> 7. Men in Black		$ 4,204,505	 $225,304,729</p>
<p> 8. Picture Perfect	   $ 3,322,480	 $ 23,739,190</p>
<p> 9. Contact		     $ 2,872,875	 $ 88,581,422</p>
<p>10. How To Be A Player	$ 2,527,810	 $ 10,015,681</p>
<p>&quot;Cop Land&quot; is released by Miramax Films, a unit of Walt Disney Co.</p>
<p>&quot;Air Force One&quot; and &quot;Men in Black&quot; are released by Columbia Pictures, a unit of Sony Corp.</p>
<p>&quot;Conspiracy Theory&quot; and &quot;Contact&quot; are released by Warner Bros., a unit of Time Warner Inc.</p>
<p>&quot;Event Horizon&quot; is released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc.</p>
<p>&quot;Spawn&quot; is released by New Line Cinema, a unit of Time Warner Inc.</p>
<p>&quot;George of the Jungle&quot; is released by Disney.</p>
<p>&quot;Picture Perfect&quot; is released by 20th Century Fox, a unit of News Corp.</p>
<p>&quot;Def Jam's How To Be A Player&quot; is released by Gramercy Pictures, a unit of PolyGram NV.</p>
<p>.</p>
